  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1004.02 Eligible Applicants and Purposes of Funding",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1004.02 Eligible Applicants and Purposes of Funding.\n\n(a) A political subdivision or other government entity that is in compliance with the hazardous waste rules shall be eligible to apply for a grant from the HWCF for costs associated with:\n\n(1) The establishment or improvement of household DIY used oil collection centers; and\n\n(2) The offsite transportation and recycling of household DIY used oil.\n\n(b) A non-profit organization that focuses on waste management and recycling issues, or a private business that is a registered state motor vehicle inspection station, shall be eligible to apply for a grant from the HWCF for costs to establish a household DIY used oil collection center, provided the organization or business is in compliance with the hazardous waste rules.\n\n(c) Grant awards shall not exceed $2,500 on an annual basis.\n\n(d) Political subdivisions that use the same household DIY used oil collection center may combine grant awards, however in no case shall the grant awarded to a household DIY used oil collection center exceed $5,000.\n\nSource. #14284, eff 8-1-25, EXPIRES: 8-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1000.html"
